    { id: "s2-check", title: "Check it", detail: "In DevTools, confirm the list is <ul> with <li> children (not divs or line breaks). Then read the section aloud in your head top-to-bottom: each ingredient should make sense on its own line. If a screen reader would announce 'list, 6 items', you're good.", estimatedMinutes: 5 }
  ] },
  { id: "s3-keyboard", title: "Session 3 — Keyboard navigation", detail: "Make every interactive element reachable and operable by keyboard only: focusable links/buttons with a visible focus outline, logical tab order, and no keyboard traps. Add a 'Jump to instructions' skip link at the top. Deliverable: a page you can fully operate with Tab / Shift+Tab / Enter / Space.", estimatedMinutes: 25, outcomes: ["Ensure all controls are keyboard-reachable with a visible focus indicator", "Add a skip link and confirm logical tab order"], children: [
    { id: "s3-check", title: "Check it", detail: "Close the mouse. Press Tab from the top: the skip link should be first, then controls in visual order, each showing a clear focus ring. Press Enter/Space to activate each. Confirm Shift+Tab goes backwards and nothing traps focus. If any control is unreachable or its focus is invisible, fix it.", estimatedMinutes: 5 }
  ] },
  { id: "s4-screenreader", title: "Session 4 — Final screen reader check", detail: "Run the whole page through a screen reader and fix what it reveals. Deliverable: a page that reads cleanly end-to-end with correct order, list announcements, and no missing labels.", estimatedMinutes: 25, outcomes: ["Verify reading order, list and heading announcements, and labelled controls with a real screen reader", "Fix any issues the reader surfaces"], children: [
